 r←Test_Misc_042(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;tv;hadHome;home;qdmx;filename
⍝ `CreateConfigFile` reports a clear error when the Cider package has no folder on disk any more,
⍝ which shows as an empty `TatinVars.HOME` (issue #136). It used to fail with a FILE NAME ERROR
⍝ on "/cider.config.template". `TatinVars.HOME` is emptied for the test and restored afterwards.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 tempDir←∆GetFolderInTempDir⊃⎕SI
 filename←tempDir,'/cider.config'
 tv←##.Cider.TatinVars
 hadHome←2=tv.⎕NC'HOME'
 :If hadHome
     home←tv.HOME
 :EndIf
 tv.HOME←''

 :Trap 11
     {}##.Cider.CreateConfigFile filename'Foo'
     →T.GoToTidyUp 1
 :Else
     qdmx←⎕DMX
     →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'no folder on disk'⍷qdmx.EM
 :EndTrap
 →T.GoToTidyUp ⎕NEXISTS filename

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 :If hadHome
     tv.HOME←home
 :Else
     {}tv.⎕EX'HOME'
 :EndIf
 FilesAndDirs.RmDir tempDir,'/..'
⍝Done
